    "title": "LESSON 53: THE 'RE-' PREFIX",
    "header_color": "green",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "The prefix RE- means AGAIN or BACK:",
          "the action happens once more, or goes",
          "back to where it came from.",
          "",
          "AGAIN:                                Press 1",
          "legi     → relegi     = read → reread",
          "fari     → refari     = do → redo",
          "kontakti → rekontakti = contact again",
          "",
          "BACK:                                 Press 2",
          "veni     → reveni     = come → come back",
          "doni     → redoni     = give → give back",
          "sendi    → resendi    = send → send back",
          "",
          "IN USE:                               Press 3",
          "Mi revenos al la temo morgaŭ.",
          "= I'll come back to the topic tomorrow.",
          "Ĝis revido! = Goodbye! (Till we meet again!)"
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Legi. Relegi. Fari. Refari. Kontakti. Rekontakti.",
          "2": "Veni. Reveni. Doni. Redoni. Sendi. Resendi.",
          "3": "Mi revenos al la temo morgaŭ. Ĝis revido!"
        },
        "pronunciation": "Leciono kvindek du"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "048",
