    "header_color": "green",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "ESTI + an active participle builds",
          "compound tenses. You RARELY need them:",
          "the simple verb already says it all.",
          "",
          "THE NORMAL WAY:                       Press 1",
          "Mi legas. = I read. / I'm reading.",
          "Mi legis. = I read. / I was reading. /",
          "            I have read.",
          "Mi legos. = I'll read. / I'll be reading.",
          "",
          "COMPOUND = FOR EMPHASIS ONLY:         Press 2",
          "Mi estas leganta.",
          "= I'm (right in the middle of) reading.",
          "Mi jam estis manĝinta, kiam vi venis.",
          "= I had already eaten when you came.",
          "Don't use 'estas leganta' for every",
          "English 'is reading': it sounds odd."
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Mi legas. Mi legis. Mi legos.",
          "2": "Mi estas leganta. Mi jam estis manĝinta, kiam vi venis."
        },
        "pronunciation": "Leciono kvardek sep"
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "THE PASSIVE IS DIFFERENT: ESTI + -ITA",
          "(or -ATA) is the everyday passive.",
          "",
          "ONE PARTICIPLE, EVERY TENSE:          Press 1",
          "La salono estas rezervita. = is booked",
