  {
    "lesson_id": "049",
    "trigger_word": "respondeco",
    "title": "LESSON 56: THE '-END-' SUFFIX",
    "header_color": "green",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "The suffix -END- means \"must be done\" or",
          "\"to be done\" (necessity/obligation).",
          "",
          "OBLIGATION:",
          "fari    → farenda     = do → to be done",
          "pagi    → pagenda     = pay → to be paid",
          "legi    → legenda     = read → to be read",
          "lerni   → lernenda    = learn → to be learned",
          "",
          "COMPARE WITH -IND-:",
          "-ind- = WORTH doing (value judgment)",
          "-end- = MUST BE done (necessity)",
          "leginda = worth reading (optional)",
          "legenda = must be read (required)",
          "",
          "IN USE:",
          "La raporto estas farenda ĝis vendredo.",
          "(The report must be done by Friday.)"
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Leciono kvardek naŭ"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "050",
    "trigger_word": "parkumado",
    "title": "LESSON 57: THE '-UM-' SUFFIX",
    "header_color": "green",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "The suffix -UM- has NO fixed meaning.",
          "It links a root to a related idea, and",
          "each word is learned on its own.",
          "",
          "COMMON -UM- WORDS:                    Press 1",
          "parko   → parkumi    = park → to park (a car)",
          "plena   → plenumi    = full → to carry out",
          "kolo    → kolumo     = neck → collar",
          "butono  → butonumi   = button → to button",
          "brako   → brakumi    = arm → to hug",
          "aero    → aerumi     = air → to air out",
          "komuna  → komunumo   = common → community",
          "",
          "IN USE:                               Press 2",
          "Kie mi povas parkumi?",
          "= Where can I park?",
          "Mi plenumis mian promeson.",
          "= I kept my promise."
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Parko. Parkumi. Plena. Plenumi. Kolo. Kolumo. Butono. Butonumi. Brako. Brakumi. Aero. Aerumi. Komuna. Komunumo.",
          "2": "Kie mi povas parkumi? Mi plenumis mian promeson."
        },
        "pronunciation": "Leciono kvindek"
      }
    ]
  }
